-- Review of the find / verify / cities runs of 2026-11-04/05 (PRs #379-#387).
-- Olive Branch MS (new, published): MS Mahj's site is titled "American Mah Jongg Lessons & Events" and its event pages say its instructor "teaches American Mah Jongg at beginner through advanced levels" (read by the research server; our fetch of msmahj.com is reset by the site; Mahjong 4 Friends also lists Linda McKnight as teaching NMJL). Sessions are at public venues (a yarn shop, a game store, a grocery, a golf resort) in Olive Branch, Horn Lake, Southaven and Tunica.
-- New York / Durham / Marin: rows that were directory-only NEEDS_REVIEW are promoted on their own pages (Bryant Park social "National Mah Jongg League style"; Durham County Library "the current National Mahjong League card"; Dana Lange's site "American Mah Jongg is the game everyone loves"; Marinwood CSD course on the NMJL card; Carol Neel).
-- New unpublished cities with one or two ACTIVE rows each: Oakland (JCC East Bay), San Jose (Camden Community Center open play), Danville (Town of Danville class, Bay Area Mahj, Jean Melgar), East Hills (Sid Jacobson JCC) and East Meadow (Town of Hempstead). Sid Jacobson JCC and Congregation Rodeph Sholom stay NEEDS_REVIEW (member-only wording). The Orlando Ocean Prime night is Mahj & Away's.
-- Held: Johnson County KS (JCPRD says "bring your own card", no American / NMJL wording), Santa Maria ("National Mah Jongg rules" only), Saratoga Springs SUNY course (full, ends today), the rest report-only.
